{
  "an8.55:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 8.55 ",
  "an8.55:0.2": "6. Gotamī ",
  "an8.55:0.3": "With Ujjaya ",
  "an8.55:1.1": "Then Ujjaya the brahmin went up to the Buddha, and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "an8.55:1.2": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side and said to the Buddha: ",
  "an8.55:1.3": "“Worthy Gotama, we wish to travel abroad. ",
  "an8.55:1.4": "May the Buddha please teach us the Dhamma in a way that leads to our welfare and happiness in this life and lives to come.” ",
  "an8.55:2.1": "“Brahmin, these four things lead to the welfare and happiness of a gentleman in this life. ",
  "an8.55:2.2": "What four? ",
  "an8.55:2.3": "Accomplishment in initiative, protection, good friendship, and balanced finances. ",
  "an8.55:3.1": "And what is accomplishment in initiative? ",
  "an8.55:3.2": "It’s when a gentleman earns a living by means such as ",
  "an8.55:3.3": "farming, trade, raising cattle, archery, government service, or one of the professions. ",
  "an8.55:3.4": "He understands how to go about these things in order to complete and organize the work. ",
  "an8.55:3.5": "This is called accomplishment in initiative. ",
  "an8.55:4.1": "And what is accomplishment in protection? ",
  "an8.55:4.2": "It’s when a gentleman owns legitimate wealth that he has earned by his own efforts and initiative, built up with his own hands, gathered by the sweat of the brow. ",
  "an8.55:4.3": "He ensures it is guarded and protected, thinking: ",
  "an8.55:4